WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.007
Outreach is for reaching people who have not messaged you yet. The app sends a small number each day, from your own browser, at a pace that keeps your account safe.

00:00:10.157 --> 00:00:16.389
Open Outreach in the menu. There are five tabs. We will go through them in the order you use them.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:29.661
Prospects are the people you want to message. Paste a list of Instagram usernames, or upload a spreadsheet. Extra columns, like a first name or a city, can be used inside your messages.

00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:44.085
A campaign is what you say to a list. Write at least five different versions of your first message. The app rotates them evenly, so no two people in a row get the same words, and you can see which version gets the most replies.

00:00:44.235 --> 00:00:57.463
Sending and typing sets the pace. The app starts at ten messages a day and builds up slowly, only inside the hours you choose, with uneven gaps between them. It will never go above fifty a day.

00:00:57.613 --> 00:01:11.759
Conversation starters bring people to you, through Instagram's official tools. When someone comments a keyword on your post, they get a private reply in their messages. And you can make trackable links that open a chat with you.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:19.677
Overview is where you switch outreach on, and see what was sent today, what is next, and how each message version is doing.

00:01:19.827 --> 00:01:29.066
If Instagram ever shows a warning, or two sends fail in one day, everything pauses by itself, and nothing restarts until you press Resume.
